      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرَصُّ</span></b>  A man <i>whose teeth are near together:</i>
(M, A, K:) fem. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَصَّآءُ</span>. (M, A.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And the fem.,
applied to a woman, <i>Impervia coëunti;</i> as also
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَصُوصٌ</span></b> . (M.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَصَّآءُ الفَخِذِيْنِ</span> A woman
<i>whose thighs are close together.</i> (A.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَخِذٌ رَصَّآءُ</span>
<i>A thigh that cleaves,</i> or <i>sticks, to its fellow.</i>
(O, K.)

